---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArtCanvas from '../components/ArtCanvas.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Seeking Zima" description="About Anilkumar Panda and the meaning behind Seeking Zima.">
  <div class="max-w-[860px] mx-auto px-6 py-14">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-[40px] tracking-[-0.8px] text-ink mb-8">About</h1>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-10">
      <div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-5 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          I'm Anil — a Principal Data Scientist based in Weesp, Netherlands.
          I build ML systems during the day and side projects at night.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work sits at the intersection of machine learning, product thinking,
          and creative tooling. I'm interested in how AI can augment human judgment
          rather than replace it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-[22px] tracking-[-0.3px] text-ink pt-4">Why "Seeking Zima"?</h2>
        <p>
          In <em>Love, Death & Robots</em>, Zima is a robot who started as a simple
          pool-cleaning machine. Over centuries of upgrades he became the most famous
          artist in the universe. But at his final exhibition, he stripped away all
          his upgrades one by one, dived into a pool, and returned to his original
          purpose — cleaning tiles. Just a small robot doing the one simple thing it
          was made for, completely at peace.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site is my version of that. Strip away everything unnecessary. Return to making.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="aspect-[3/4] rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <ArtCanvas id="about-art" class="w-full h-full" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
